# D18 containers and D19 Kubernetes. Everything is read from the host; nothing is executed inside containers.
@phase 1600
[D18-001] FUNC kit 120
cmd: container_runtime_detect
out: runtimes.txt
purpose: Detect container runtimes and sockets: Docker, Podman (root and rootless per user), containerd, CRI-O, LXC/LXD/Incus, systemd-nspawn; client/daemon versions.
expect: One line per runtime with socket, version, data folder.
empty: 'no container runtime' on hosts without containers.
value: Decides which of the following items apply.
ref: draft-7

[D18-002] FUNC kit 3600
cmd: docker_collect
out: docker
req: [ -S /var/run/docker.sock ] || [ -S /run/docker.sock ] || [ -d /var/lib/docker ]
purpose: Docker: version/info, containers incl. stopped (ps -a), inspect of every container/image/network/volume, logs with timestamps, diff, top, history --no-trunc of every image, events of the last --since days, compose labels -> compose files, containers.csv summary.
expect: docker/containers.csv plus docker/<container>/{inspect.json,logs.txt,diff.txt,top.txt,network/...} and docker/images/<id>.history.txt.
empty: Not applicable without Docker. Kit client falls back to a lower API version or the server's docker for old daemons.
value: Container state and lifecycle, privileged/host-network/docker.sock mounts, files changed inside containers, rebuilt Dockerfile steps.
sensitive: yes
ref: draft-7; draft-13.4; draft-37.3 no.34

[D18-003] FUNC kit 3600
cmd: container_namespaces
out: container-inside
purpose: For every running container (any runtime): network inside its namespace (ip addr/route/neigh, ss, iptables/nft) via nsenter -n, and key files read through /proc/<pid>/root (passwd, shadow, crontabs, shell histories, authorized_keys, resolv.conf, hosts, hostname, os-release).
expect: container-inside/<name>/network/*.txt and files/... copies.
empty: EMPTY when no container runs.
value: Backdoors and attacker activity inside containers without docker exec (no state change).
sensitive: yes
ref: draft-13.4; draft-7

[D18-004] COPY kit 7200
cmd: -R /var/lib/docker/containers /etc/docker /etc/containerd /etc/crio /etc/containers /var/lib/containers/storage/overlay-containers /etc/systemd/system/docker.service.d /etc/default/docker /etc/sysconfig/docker
purpose: Raw Docker/containerd/CRI-O/Podman configuration and per-container state files (config.v2.json, hostconfig.json, *-json.log).
expect: Per-container folders and daemon configuration.
empty: Not applicable without these runtimes.
value: Ground truth when the daemon is down or lies; full container logs including rotations.
sensitive: yes
ref: draft-7

[D18-005] FUNC kit 3600
cmd: compose_dockerfiles_search
out: build-files
purpose: Search the filesystem for Dockerfile*, Containerfile*, *.dockerfile, docker-compose*/compose*.y?ml, .dockerignore, podman-compose, Helm charts, kustomization and Kubernetes manifests; copy them with the .env next to compose files.
expect: build-files/found.tsv and copies. Rows say NOT FOUND per category when nothing exists.
empty: EMPTY when no build/deploy files exist.
value: How containers were built and deployed; secrets in .env; attacker-modified compose files.
sensitive: yes
ref: draft-13.4

[D18-006] FUNC mixed 3600
cmd: podman_collect
out: podman
req: has podman || [ -d /var/lib/containers ] || ls -d /home/*/.local/share/containers >/dev/null 2>&1
purpose: Podman (root through the server's podman; rootless per user from storage files): ps -a, inspect, logs, images, volumes.
expect: podman/... per user.
empty: Not applicable without Podman.
value: Rootless containers are invisible to root's docker command.
sensitive: yes
ref: draft-28.3 no.24

[D18-007] FUNC kit 1800
cmd: containerd_cri_collect
out: containerd-cri
req: [ -S /run/containerd/containerd.sock ] || [ -S /var/run/crio/crio.sock ] || [ -S /run/k3s/containerd/containerd.sock ]
purpose: containerd (ctr per namespace: containers, tasks, images, snapshots) and CRI (crictl ps -a, pods, inspect, logs, images); falls back to ctr where crictl is unavailable (armv7).
expect: containerd-cri/<ns>/... and cri/... files.
empty: Not applicable without containerd/CRI-O.
value: Kubernetes node workloads and plain containerd containers.
sensitive: yes
ref: draft-7; draft-37.3 no.36

[D18-008] FUNC server 1200
cmd: lxc_nspawn_collect
out: lxc-nspawn
req: has lxc || has lxc-ls || has incus || has machinectl || [ -d /var/lib/lxc ]
purpose: LXC/LXD/Incus (list, info --show-log, config) and systemd-nspawn machines.
expect: Per-container info and logs.
empty: Not applicable without these tools.
value: System containers hosting services or hidden environments.
ref: draft-7

